100`t/// Editor-owned interaction contract for the top-level block drag handle.
101`t///
102`t/// The handle is row chrome: it belongs to the editor's top-level block shell,
103`t/// not to [BlockRendererBuilder] output. Keeping the contract here lets custom
104`t/// renderers rely on the same menu/reorder surface without wrapping their own
105`t/// handle, and keeps nested surfaces (table cells, inline embeds, object-block
106`t/// controls) out of row-sorting hit testing.
107`tabstract final class BlockDragHandleSpec {
108`t  /// Reserved leading gutter for the handle, outside the renderer's content box.
109`t  static const double railWidth = 32.0;
110`t
111`t  /// Gap between the renderer content edge and the handle hit target.
112`t  static const double gapToContent = 4.0;
113`t
114`t  /// Minimum pointer/focus hit target for mouse, touch, and keyboard traversal.
115`t  static const Size hitSize = Size.square(28.0);
116`t
117`t  /// Visual glyph size inside [hitSize].
